  "metadata": {
    "title": "CTAmap: A continuous vector dataset of Chinese administrative divisions from 2000 to 2026",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22179207",
    "publication_date": "2026-08-30",
    "description": "<p>CTAmap is a continuous vector dataset of Chinese administrative divisions covering the period from 2000 to 2026. It provides topologically consistent administrative boundaries at the provincial, prefectural, and county levels. The dataset is constructed using a \"hybrid reconstruction framework\" that integrates the 2020 national baseline vector with underlying micro-level spatial units (township and village vectors) to accurately reconstruct historical spatial reorganizations. All boundary units are strictly matched with the official statutory records and the 6-digit administrative division codes published by the Ministry of Civil Affairs of China. It serves as a spatial baseline for long-term Earth system science, historical census data integration, and spatial downscaling analyses.</p>\n<p><strong>Folder Structure</strong>: The dataset package is organized as follows:</p>\n<p>- <em>`T{YYYY}_{level}.gpkg`</em> (81 files): The spatial vector data in GeoPackage format &mdash; one file per year and level.<br>- <em>`shp_2000-2013.zip` / `shp_2014-2026.zip`</em>: The spatial vector data in standard Shapefile format, bundled by period. Each bundle contains one single-year archive per year (`shp_T{YYYY}.zip`), which in turn holds the three Shapefile layers of that year.<br>- <em>`tables.zip`</em>: The event table, document index, feature&ndash;document links, validation tables, data dictionary, and file inventory.<br>- <em>`logs.zip`</em>: The annual modification logs. This includes detailed textual records of administrative division changes, tracking the historical evolution and providing official evidence for spatial reconstructions.</p>\n<p><strong>Temporal and Hierarchical Organization</strong>: Within the GeoPackage files and the Shapefile archives, the data is structured chronologically and hierarchically:</p>\n<p>- 27 continuous snapshots, named from 2000 to 2026 (`T{YYYY}`), where the year-Y layer represents the administrative status at 00:00 on 1 January of year Y (i.e., the end of year Y&minus;1).<br>- Three administrative levels within each snapshot:<br>&nbsp; - `province` &mdash; Provincial-level administrative boundaries (e.g., provinces, autonomous regions, municipalities).<br>&nbsp; - `prefecture` &mdash; Prefectural-level administrative boundaries (e.g., prefecture-level cities, autonomous prefectures).<br>&nbsp; - `county` &mdash; County-level administrative boundaries (e.g., counties, districts, county-level cities).</p>",
